      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.23244_p5_b19",
      "text": "What COALA optimizes.\nCOALA does not perform\ngradient-based updates to the pretrained language model\nweights. Instead, it freezes the base LLM and learns a\nconvex neural network (cvxNN) head on top of frozen pre-\ntrained features. This design is deliberate: by restricting\noptimization to the convex head, we obtain global opti-\nmality guarantees for the trained preference module, sub-\nstantially reduce memory and compute requirements, and\npreserve a practical single-GPU training regime. Conse-\nquently, COALA should be interpreted as a preference align-\nment framework built on top of frozen LLM representations,\nrather than as full-model policy optimization in the style of\nstandard DPO fine-tuning.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.08,
        484.23,
        291.1,
        637.82
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        220,
        1936,
        1164,
        2551
      ],
